===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|NL.|{{taxfmt|Orchideae|tribe}}}}, {{taxfmt|Orchidaceae|family}}, an irregular formation from {{der|en|la|orchis}}, from {{der|en|grc|ὄρχις|t=orchid, testicle}} (ostensibly from the shape of the roots<ref>{{R:LSJ|ὄρχις}}</ref>). Supplanted {{noncog|enm|ballokwort|lit=testicle plant}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɔː.kɪd/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-orchid.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɔɹ.kɪd/|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)kɪd|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q25308}}A plant of the orchid family ({{taxfmt|Orchidaceae|family}}), bearing unusually-shaped [[flower]]s of beautiful colours. {{defdate|mid-19th c.}}
# A light [[blue|bluish]]-[[red]], [[violet]]-red or [[purple]] [[color|colour]].
#: {{color panel|DA70D6}}

